                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "014bdade-9a88-3af6-afb9-da45e294d58a",
                        "entry_id": "b55aca5c-8043-3211-9543-524e78128f48",
                        "glosses": [
                            "das erneute Auftreten einer zeitweilig erfolgreich behandelten Krankheit"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff2bee02-6034-4464-91bb-c8f5075065db",
                                "sense_id": "014bdade-9a88-3af6-afb9-da45e294d58a",
                                "text": "Tritt ein entfernter Tumor an der gleichen Stelle wieder auf, spricht man von einem lokalen Rezidiv."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c3e95fb7-5b5c-4a8d-b9a3-23b5c5fd215e",
                        "source_entry_id": "b55aca5c-8043-3211-9543-524e78128f48",
                        "source_sense_id": "014bdade-9a88-3af6-afb9-da45e294d58a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Medizin: das erneute Auftreten einer zeitweilig erfolgreich behandelten Krankheit",
                        "target_lang_word": "recidive",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "recidive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8fc6a58-3400-3cf4-9859-d7cf84669141",
                                        "entry_id": "16d7727a-44af-34e8-a65c-faf8636c31da",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of recidivous (“recurring”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "063d96a2-cf44-4367-91bf-360c8951e577",
                                                "sense_id": "b8fc6a58-3400-3cf4-9859-d7cf84669141",
                                                "text": "But the truth is, as I haue oft ſeene, that this forme doth nothing, ſaue onely hide the ſicknes, and appeaſe the dolors for a time, ſo that it is alwayes recidiue, and oſt times by the long and violent vſage heereof, the humors are rendred more drying, maling, and burned, of the which come miſerable ſimptoms, as I haue often ſeene."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75bdd028-3e23-4ea7-9baa-fd21a2a6fc3d",
                                                "sense_id": "b8fc6a58-3400-3cf4-9859-d7cf84669141",
                                                "text": "[T]he evil humours remaining after a Criſe, are wont to make one recidive or relapſing; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "798db0d6-0fae-4651-91f9-0a89e6cfec29",
                                                "sense_id": "b8fc6a58-3400-3cf4-9859-d7cf84669141",
                                                "text": "It was the second case of recidive calculus which I had operated on since my arrival in England; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14120892-fac2-42ee-8309-e764128aa7ee",
                                                "sense_id": "b8fc6a58-3400-3cf4-9859-d7cf84669141",
                                                "text": "If any suspicion of recidive aldosteronism was present, patients were carefully reexamined by hormonal tests and computed tomography (CT)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f22bdc04-1fd6-3149-8830-126a8434cd30",
                                        "entry_id": "16d7727a-44af-34e8-a65c-faf8636c31da",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of recidivous (“prone to relapse”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "808f4d77-25d7-49a0-bb9d-6f0b5dd329b7",
                                                "sense_id": "f22bdc04-1fd6-3149-8830-126a8434cd30",
                                                "text": "[H]is maieste had never remembred their precedent offenses nor imputed thesame^([sic]) to their charge, Being a prince most honorable obseruatour of his worde . But seing their cankred recidive hert he could no lesse doo then to suffre them to have his lawes . to thexemple of suche Ingrate and Irremediable obstinate hertes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cc5f71b-e20b-4b40-b906-506df4c02a11",
                                                "sense_id": "f22bdc04-1fd6-3149-8830-126a8434cd30",
                                                "text": "He was, then, already a recidive offender when he came here for the first time, and he has been here 4, and not three times, as the press says."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70b13fbf-cc01-4b65-8e79-7d66fedef3a0",
                                                "sense_id": "f22bdc04-1fd6-3149-8830-126a8434cd30",
                                                "text": "Charlemagne went further, punishing the recidive thief by death and providing that authors of crimes against good morals might, for the first offence, be handed over to the judgment of the bishop, and, if that did not suffice for their correction and their fault was grave, they should suffer confiscation of their allodial lands."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "recidive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd2a66e6-4006-3599-8e79-2557af1eaaaf",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb09de9-ac3b-3536-b536-4947fd0d783d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of recidivation (“relapse”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "110b5dbc-9fc7-421a-96f4-87378ef281ae",
                                                "sense_id": "dd2a66e6-4006-3599-8e79-2557af1eaaaf",
                                                "text": "Take alwaies heede to the forces of the ſick, & beware of that which is cauſe of all dolors and recidiues: that is, the number of the frictions, by reaſon that ſome giue ouer-few, fearing theſe accidents, and to the contrary, ſome others that gyue ouer-many, in ſuch ſort that I haue heard men vaunt themſelues, to haue rubbed the poore Patient 37. times."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1843e286-af8a-45af-8db2-628b151c0ee2",
                                                "sense_id": "dd2a66e6-4006-3599-8e79-2557af1eaaaf",
                                                "text": "But this was like the palliative cure of a ſore, & a lightning for the preſent of a ſick bodie: wherby it might ſoone after by relapſe fall backe, as it were, into a recidive, and a worſe diſeaſe and more daungerous than the other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa5f73f0-cd62-4b25-bf39-9d613d5a4cf8",
                                                "sense_id": "dd2a66e6-4006-3599-8e79-2557af1eaaaf",
                                                "text": "The recidive is the greatest obstacle of this disease, because the yeast usually returns after the long treatment period."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b07108b-efb0-340d-929d-f7cbaeb8be60",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb09de9-ac3b-3536-b536-4947fd0d783d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of recidivist (“one who falls back into prior habits”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d01aef2e-60a9-4817-a56f-1ecfc1951ac3",
                                                "sense_id": "7b07108b-efb0-340d-929d-f7cbaeb8be60",
                                                "text": "The severity of Jansenism could hardly be a greater guarantee for repentance than the mild discipline of the Church, when it was compatible with the impenitence of [Jean François Paul de Gondi, Cardinal] de Retz, and the feeble penance of such a recidive as Anne de Rohan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b83d22e3-3eba-4100-bbe2-0247548022ba",
                                                "sense_id": "7b07108b-efb0-340d-929d-f7cbaeb8be60",
                                                "text": "It is the great dominant question of the recidive, the habitual offender, the criminal class. In his lurid romance, “Les Misérables,” Victor Hugo has canonized the innocent recidive, Jean Valjean, who is not the enemy but the victim of law and order."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ea2ad4e-ffdf-47f2-9575-4136f98452bd",
                                                "sense_id": "7b07108b-efb0-340d-929d-f7cbaeb8be60",
                                                "text": "The fixed punitive sentence should become a practice of the past. There should be substituted the indeterminate sentence with two types of institutions—one for the first offenders and one for the recidives."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "recidive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6bcf7d5-d0c9-3695-b5ba-348a1f8e8d33",
                                        "entry_id": "942bc79f-e01d-3ff1-ab4a-ae3bf23092ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of recidivate (“to fall back into prior habits”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85f5d3f9-0403-4b47-81a0-f56196ae9ac6",
                                                "sense_id": "d6bcf7d5-d0c9-3695-b5ba-348a1f8e8d33",
                                                "text": "Agayne if he ofte tymes recidiuyng, and fallyng into the ſame diſeaſe agayne, be at the length with muche a doe rid ⁊ healed therof, thẽ doth he the moꝛe hate his diſeaſe, and alſo the moꝛe knowledge the benefite of his healing, and ſhall better knowe how to cure other that are lykewiſe diſeaſed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cb9e8c3-47ff-44e1-93fa-7837e6db8433",
                                                "sense_id": "d6bcf7d5-d0c9-3695-b5ba-348a1f8e8d33",
                                                "text": "‘I’d walk out today if I had the courage.’ / ‘Ah, but then you’re probably a first offender, while Judith and I are recidivists. Am I right?’ / ‘And how!’ Judith laughed. ‘What’s more I’m going on recidiving just as soon as I kick the dust of this place off my heels.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22f652e4-c6d3-479f-b2aa-a3205506e615",
                                                "sense_id": "d6bcf7d5-d0c9-3695-b5ba-348a1f8e8d33",
                                                "text": "Weekends I recidived / Into Alma Mater."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5de86dd6-8703-4603-a98a-f184e7cc0f95",
                                                "sense_id": "d6bcf7d5-d0c9-3695-b5ba-348a1f8e8d33",
                                                "text": "We see that the probability levels off above 0.6. Thus, there may be about this proportion of people who will not recidive."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "243f4f85-d9bf-4648-808e-bf5da639c655",
                        "source_entry_id": "b55aca5c-8043-3211-9543-524e78128f48",
                        "source_sense_id": "014bdade-9a88-3af6-afb9-da45e294d58a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Medizin: das erneute Auftreten einer zeitweilig erfolgreich behandelten Krankheit",
                        "target_lang_word": "récidive",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "récidive",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eeb06053-59d4-3c14-89a8-a749f0a6f22f",
                                        "entry_id": "bf1dc9d1-79cf-3155-a7ea-3b73f5262581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rechute dans une faute ; action de commettre de nouveau le même délit, le même crime."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8019581-7873-4a39-9fea-f2372676f600",
                                                "sense_id": "eeb06053-59d4-3c14-89a8-a749f0a6f22f",
                                                "text": "La prison devrait être une école de la réinsertion, elle devient une école de la récidive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e9fb010-28f5-49cb-92b5-1f0008a0d595",
                                                "sense_id": "eeb06053-59d4-3c14-89a8-a749f0a6f22f",
                                                "text": "Les lois qui frappent la récidive correctionnelle ne font pas, en effet, de distinction entre la récidive locale et la récidive encourue en divers points du territoire de la République."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15a925c6-6e37-46f4-a738-4528ee8a9688",
                                                "sense_id": "eeb06053-59d4-3c14-89a8-a749f0a6f22f",
                                                "text": "Être accusé de vol avec récidive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64e4600b-8ee3-446e-a28a-12a969aa093b",
                                                "sense_id": "eeb06053-59d4-3c14-89a8-a749f0a6f22f",
                                                "text": "Le conducteur présumé du véhicule lors des faits, un homme de 46 ans, a été mis en examen pour assassinat, délit de fuite et conduite en état alcoolique en récidive légale. Son casier judiciaire porte la mention de 13 condamnations, la plus récente pour récidive de conduite en état alcoolique en mars 2019."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17f4bd68-19f0-3f64-8bbd-7aa52255a351",
                                        "entry_id": "bf1dc9d1-79cf-3155-a7ea-3b73f5262581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Réapparition d’une maladie après une guérison en apparence complète et au bout d’un laps de temps quelquefois fort long."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3d3a7fa-1e4a-4d10-9c20-9f7f4b0521b2",
                                                "sense_id": "17f4bd68-19f0-3f64-8bbd-7aa52255a351",
                                                "text": "Ainsi, il paraît logique d’anticoaguler les patients présentant une cardiopathie à haut risque de récidive embolique : prothèses valvulaires mécaniques, valvulopathies mitrales, infarctus du myocarde récent, cardiomyopathies dilatées, anévrysmes ventriculaires, fibrillation auriculaire non rhumatismale associée à un thrombus intracavitaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bee4df0-681a-4b23-956a-cd4c49728c3d",
                                                "sense_id": "17f4bd68-19f0-3f64-8bbd-7aa52255a351",
                                                "text": "Hallopeau présenta devant l’Académie de médecine l’observation d'un homme de 35 ans atteint d’une syphilis secondaire d’abord traitée par le mercure puis par le salvarsan du fait d’une récidive. Après deux injections, le malade mourait."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6030a338-05ee-468c-b815-819c111e2b0d",
                                                "sense_id": "17f4bd68-19f0-3f64-8bbd-7aa52255a351",
                                                "text": "Compte tenu de la classification de son cancer, Lucile rechercha sur Internet les statistiques de récidive. À l’horizon de cinq ans, seulement 25 % des patients avaient survécu."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
